Z||000005||87GTZ34||05-14-2001||01:02 AM||||I've found Carparts to have a lot of 'typos'.  Best bet is to call their support to see if they can tell from the description that only they can see.  I had a guy check on their molded cooling hoses and he didn't think any of them would fit a Fiero.  I ordered them anyway as they have a return policy that would allow me to return them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BC-GT||05-14-2001||01:05 AM||||from Edelbrocks site:<P>SPRINT CAR HEADERS<BR> <BR>Designed for aluminum spread-port heads, our headers have one-piece 5/16" header flanges that clear fuel injection nozzles and water temperature heat sensors with no cutting. Flanges are surface ground. Available with 1-7/8" or 2" primaries and 3-1/2" collectors. Designed with a forward sweep to allow easy installation of the silencer between the collector and rear tire. <P>1-7/8" primaries (pair) #6820 <BR>2" primaries (pair) #6821 <BR>1-7/8" primaries (left side only for 4-cylinder applications) #6819 <BR>2" primaries (left side only for 4-cylinder applications) #6818 <P>&gt;&gt;&gt;Aluminum  spread-port heads??? Thats not a stock 2.8 is it?||||reg||1
Z||000007||BC-GT||05-14-2001||11:45 AM||||Just talked to tech support at Edelbrock and they don't make any header's for the Fiero,period. To bad.||||reg||1
