Z||000011||Oreif||05-15-2001||10:31 AM||||The edelbrock "sprint" headers are designed for "Sprint" cars. The sprint racing cars. The sprints use 4-cyl for the Under 3.0L class and V-6's for the over 3.0L class.<BR>(Basically 2.3's and 2.5's for the 4-cyl and 3.1/3.3's for the V-6 class) These are GM engines and they have different designed heads than what's on a production motor. I went to a sprint race car building site and if you buy the headers you'll need to remove the drivers side tire to fit the headers. I think carparts.com is confused. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fiero_Freak||05-15-2001||11:41 PM||||If they do work try summit racing... they are $171 there...but it does just describe them as 2" sprint headers.||||reg||1
Z||000013||BBBAD GT||05-16-2001||12:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BC-GT:<BR><B>from Edelbrocks site:<P>SPRINT CAR HEADERS<BR> <BR> Available with 1-7/8" or 2" primaries and 3-1/2" collectors. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Do you know how big these headers are?  They would be horrible for anything under 4k rpms.  Heck, I'm only running 1 5/8" shorty headers and 2.5" dual exhaust on my 500+ hp 5.0, and I'd definately lose a ton of torque down low if I went with 1 7/8" headers, just think what it would do to a 135 hp motor.<BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
